s10-8-p2 : Block
s10-8-p2 = prose (cons "Unison provides a concrete precedent for treating program definitions as structured, content-addressed objects rather than source files whose mutable names supply their identity ([42](#ref-42), [43](#ref-43)). In a content-addressed codebase, a definition is stored with its typed syntax tree and dependency references. A name is a view or alias; a stable reference identifies a particular definition. The immediate advantage is that dependencies and reuse refer to the actual definitions involved, so renaming does not rewrite the computation. A change to a definition produces a new object and determines precisely which dependent constructions may require recomputation." nil)
